    {
      "id": "claim_922dbe3ab48e46469c8a35be949aef5a",
      "statement": "On disk, a project stores only schema and paper metadata in project.json; every reviewer's and the consolidated annotation answers live in a sibling annotations/<paperId>/ folder, one file per reviewer plus a consolidated file. The split was introduced to avoid git-merge conflicts between reviewers editing the same all-in-one file. The renderer keeps the logical whole-project shape: DesktopAdapter.saveProject does the send, and the Rust project.rs::write_project_files performs the split, writing each annotation file inside the project (refusing paths that escape it and the reserved feedback/ directory), while the read side reassembles a split project back into that logical text before handing it to the renderer.",
